  "status_text": "The same graph handles every choice of weights for its rules, just by switching dots on or off. Lean checked this for a fixed list of partial bit patterns and any modulus M of at least two. Pin the input bits and keep each designated switch dot exactly when its binary weight digit is one. Count selections with those pins and no line between any two selected dots. Modulo M, this count equals the sum of the weights of matching patterns, counting repeats. With n pins and b digits per weight, each path bag contains all pins and at most 2n+3b+5 dots (L-lib-1234).",
